  abstract  = {REPORT] Inventory Record #83 Integrating Deep Learning into Clinical Decision-Making for Lumbar Degenerative Disease on MRI Authors: Baoyi Ke, Wenyu Ma, Junbo Xuan, Yinghao Liang, Liguang Zhou, Wenyong Jiang, Jing Lin, Guixiang Li Publication / Venue: Clinical research article Year: 2025 DOI: 10.3389/fsurg.2024.1424716 Primary Source URL: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/39834502/ Inventory Category: Adjacent lumbar MRI AI Comparability / Priority: Moderate | Priority: Important Study Details & Methodology from Literature Inventory Study Type / MRI View: Clinical comparison | Lumbar MRI Dataset & Cohort: None (Sample: None) Disease / Target: Normal disc, disc herniation, spondylolisthesis Model / AI Method: PP-YOLOv2-based deep learning Evaluation Metrics: Sensitivity, specificity, accuracy Key Finding / Relevance: None Thesis Context (Ch 2): Clinical decision-support framing rather than model-only benchmarking. Abstract / Summary},
  comment   = {[Abstract-only record - publisher full text not held.] PP-YOLOv2-based system identifying normal intervertebral discs, lumbar disc herniation and spondylolisthesis from lumbar MRI, framed as clinical decision support rather than a benchmark exercise. Retrospective data from January 2017 to January 2022 covered 654 patients, 604 training and 50 testing, with the test set independently annotated by three spinal specialists so model and surgeons could be compared directly. The algorithm reached mAP 90.08\% and showed higher sensitivity, specificity and accuracy than manual identification, in significantly less time (p < 0.05). The authors conclude its diagnostic performance exceeds that of most spinal surgeons. Useful for the decision-support framing, though the comparison is against surgeons rather than radiologists.},
  note      = {Thesis Citation: [Chapter 2: Chapter 2 (subsection: Benchmarking Against Clinicians)]. Thesis Importance: Provides critical context, methodology, baseline comparison, or clinical validation standard for Selar's PhD dissertation.},
}

